\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Score shifts from deterministic-mixed to LLM-only re-judge. All four students gain on both conditions; Haiku gains the most. For all three SFT'd students, $\Delta $CU $>$ $\Delta $BL by 2--4.5\,pp, meaning the deterministic judge was systematically biased \emph  {against} the curated condition --- procedure-following responses bury conclusions in narration more often than direct-thinking responses do.}}{6}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:rejudge-deltas}{{3}{6}{Score shifts from deterministic-mixed to LLM-only re-judge. All four students gain on both conditions; Haiku gains the most. For all three SFT'd students, $\Delta $CU $>$ $\Delta $BL by 2--4.5\,pp, meaning the deterministic judge was systematically biased \emph {against} the curated condition --- procedure-following responses bury conclusions in narration more often than direct-thinking responses do}{table.caption.6}{}}
